@page "/privacy"
@layout LandingPageLayout

<PageTitle>Privacy</PageTitle>

@*
    REVIEW BEFORE PUBLISHING: this describes what the code collects as of this version. The operator's name and
    contact address, the legal basis and the retention period must be filled in by whoever runs the server, and
    the text should be checked by someone qualified (GDPR, Google Play and Microsoft Store requirements).
*@

<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Medium" Class="py-8">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h4" Class="mb-4">Privacy notice</MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mt-4">What Onyx collects</MudText>
    <MudText Class="mb-2">The Onyx apps record which apps you use and for how long, so you can see it on your dashboard. For each device they upload:</MudText>
    <ul class="mb-3" style="padding-left: 1.5rem">
        <li>the name and platform of the device (for example "Pixel 9", Android), chosen when it registers;</li>
        <li>for every hour: which apps were in the foreground and for how many minutes;</li>
        <li>for each app: its identifier (package or program name), display name, category reported by the system, and icon.</li>
    </ul>
    <MudText Class="mb-2">
        Onyx does <b>not</b> record what you do inside apps: no window titles, web addresses, messages, keystrokes,
        screenshots or location. Time while the device is locked or idle for five minutes is not counted on
        computers; on Android, Onyx reads the usage history the system keeps.
    </MudText>
    <MudText Class="mb-2">
        For your account Onyx stores your user name, email address and a hash of your password (never the password
        itself), and, if you use them, phone number and two-factor settings.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mt-4">Permissions</MudText>
    <MudText Class="mb-2">
        On Android, Onyx needs "usage access", which you grant in the system settings, to read which apps were used.
        It reads the list of installed launcher apps to show their names and icons.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mt-4">Who can see it</MudText>
    <MudText Class="mb-2">
        Your usage data is visible to you when signed in, and stored on the Onyx server operated by
        <b>[operator name and contact address]</b>. It is not sold or shared with third parties. App icons are
        stored once per app and shared between accounts; they contain no personal data.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mt-4">Deleting your data</MudText>
    <MudText Class="mb-2">
        Removing a device on the Devices page deletes all usage it uploaded. Deleting your account in the profile
        settings deletes the account, all devices and all usage data. Uninstalling the app stops collection; data
        already uploaded stays until you delete it.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mt-4">Contact</MudText>
    <MudText>Questions and requests about your data: <b>[contact email]</b>.</MudText>
</MudContainer>
